This product includes software derived from CODE-A, a Fortran propagator-matrix
code for the instantaneous geoid and dynamic topography of a viscous mantle. The
method of CODE-A is described in:

  Corrieu, V., Thoraval, C. and Ricard, Y. (1995). Mantle dynamics and geoid
  Green functions. Geophysical Journal International, 120, 516-523.

  Hager, B. H. and Clayton, R. W. (1989). Constraints on the structure of mantle
  convection using seismic observations, flow models, and the geoid. In Mantle
  Convection: Plate Tectonics and Global Dynamics, ed. W. R. Peltier, Gordon and
  Breach, 657-763.

The Fortran itself, with its quad-precision LINPACK routines by John Burkardt
(LGPL), is not distributed with this product.

Parts of this product are ported from lovejx (Siavash Ghelichkhan, Jerry X.
Mitrovica, William Scott and Mark Hoggard; Apache License, Version 2.0): the
layer parameterisation of the controls, the integration of gravity from the
density profile, the pattern of the unit scales, the spherical-harmonic
conventions and the Taylor-test policy of the test suite.

